= Summary
- Presents a dialogue where a TV is capable of exploring contrafactuals.
- Questions what we allow to slip or not slip when dealing with hypothetical situations.
- Describes the processes by which a program would solve Bongard problems.
- Ponders how creativity can arise from mechanized processes.
- Presents and answers 10 questions regarding the future of AI programs.

= Dialogue $arrow.l.r.long$ Chapter Link
The dialogue explores how we have the capability to imagine different situations than reality and how some are more plausible than others.
This relates to the notions of constants, parameters, and variables.
Each describes a different level of variability which determines whether a hypothetical is possible or not.
Part of what you would want out of an AI system is the ability to imagine different scenarios and explore which ones makes reasonable sense.
This is the essence of what Bongard Problem solving programs do.

